  <p>Deciding between new construction and existing homes is one of the biggest choices military families face. Each option has unique advantages and considerations.</p>

  <h3>New Construction Advantages</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Modern features and technology</li>
    <li>Warranty protection</li>
    <li>Energy-efficient systems</li>
    <li>Customization options</li>
    <li>No hidden surprises</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Existing Home Advantages</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Established neighborhoods</li>
    <li>Mature landscaping</li>
    <li>Often better value</li>
    <li>Immediate occupancy</li>
    <li>Move-in flexibility</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Military Family Considerations</h3>
  <p>Your PCS timeline, budget, and family preferences determine the best choice. I'll help you evaluate both options based on your specific situation.</p>

  <h2>Making Your Decision</h2>
  <p>Contact me to discuss which option best fits your military family's needs and timeline.</p>
